---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/use-cases/post-purchase';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'use-cases/post-purchase');
const desc = description(site, 'use-cases/post-purchase');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does fulfillment mean delivery?",
    "answer": "No. Keep these states separate and avoid claiming arrival without a suitable signal."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should every item get a separate email?",
    "answer": "No. Combine useful resources where possible and branch only when the item needs different guidance."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should unknown gift intent be handled?",
    "answer": "Use neutral wording and shareable guides instead of assuming the buyer is the user."
  },
  {
    "question": "When should cross-sell begin?",
    "answer": "After the relevant product is received and the offer is useful, with unresolved delivery or return issues excluded."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <article class="container prose-shopify py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">All use cases</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Post-purchase email for Shopify: education after fulfillment</h1>
    <p>Build a sequence that helps buyers receive and use what they ordered. Timing should follow the relevant line item and fulfillment state, with a separate owner for order notifications.</p>
    <section class="py-8">
      <h2>Map messages to actual fulfillment</h2>
      <p>Inventory every order confirmation, shipment, delivery and pickup message before adding marketing. Shopify documents event-triggered customer notifications and controls for particular shipping updates. Identify which system sends each message; adding a lifecycle tool should not accidentally duplicate existing notifications.</p>
      <p>Keep order placement, payment, fulfillment, shipment and delivery as distinct states. A fulfilled order is not evidence that a customer has used the product. If delivery data is unavailable, use clearly conditional wording and an order-status link rather than claiming arrival. Local pickup needs its own completion signal.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="py-8">
      <h2>Teach at the line-item level</h2>
      <p>Map each product family to merchant-approved setup, care and troubleshooting resources. For a keyboard kit, identify the layout and compatible parts rather than sending a generic accessories grid. Keep instructions maintained by the product owner; an email sequence should link to authoritative guidance instead of inventing technical or safety advice.</p>
      <p>For split shipments, provide education for the item actually received. Combine compatible resources into one useful message when possible. Exclude cancelled or returned lines and account for replacements so the original purchase does not start a second, contradictory sequence.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="py-8">
      <h2>Handle gifts and uncertain ownership</h2>
      <p>Use explicit gift information where available, but do not treat a different billing and shipping address as proof of a gift. A mixed order can contain both gifts and personal purchases. Give the purchaser shareable care instructions without assuming that the recipient has joined the marketing audience.</p>
      <p>When intent is unknown, write “If this is a gift, share this guide” rather than asserting ownership. Keep buyer account links out of shareable recipient materials. Recipient communication needs its own appropriate permission and identity handling; a shipping address is not an invitation to enroll someone.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="py-8">
      <h2>Gate cross-sell on product readiness</h2>
      <p>Choose a useful next step based on compatibility, receipt and the buyer’s unresolved questions. A replacement request or open delivery problem should route to help rather than an accessory offer. Recheck stock and product compatibility at the destination as well as in the email.</p>
      <p>Separate replenishable consumables from durable-product accessories. A new order should cancel obsolete offers for the same item; it should not restart education for every product the customer has ever bought. Review requests need enough opportunity to use the product, with timing chosen for that product rather than a universal number of days.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="py-8">
      <h2>A proposed sequence review</h2>
      <p>For a split keyboard order, model one parcel delivered and another delayed. Confirm only the received component gets setup content. Add a return before the accessory message, then a replacement shipment. Inspect queued content, recipient, links and exit reason at each step. These are proposed checks, not tests we ran.</p>
      <p>Compare providers, including Sequenzy and your current stack, on this same event history. Ask which delivery signals are available, how late events are handled, and how support can stop a sequence. Measure education link use and relevant support topics alongside repeat purchase and returns; do not attribute every change to email without a comparison design.</p>
    </section>
    <p>Primary reference checked November 25, 2026: <a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/fulfillment/setup/notifications/customer-notifications">Shopify customer notification controls</a>. Workflow recommendations and proposed checks above are editorial guidance, not claims of completed testing.</p>
    <p>Continue with <a class="link" href="/use-cases/replenishment">replenishment</a>, <a class="link" href="/use-cases/reviews-and-ugc">reviews and ugc</a>. Browse the <a class="link" href="/apps">tool catalog</a> for candidates; confirm current capabilities and costs for the required integration.</p>
  </article>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Post purchase FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
